    <body>
      <div type="clause" n="17.1">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Iudex">Iudex</ref> 17.1</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="17.1"><pb n="476" ed="#liebermann"/>[Not in Q]</ab>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="ang" source="#liebermann" n="17.1" corresp="#wit-g-a"><pb n="476" ed="#liebermann"/>⁊ þa ðe him God ondrædende riht demeð<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="4" target="#Iudex_17-1.lnote.oe.4"/>, hí onfoð æt Gode éce endlean<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="c" target="#Iudex_17-1.lnote.oe.c"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="de" source="#liebermann"><pb n="476" ed="#liebermann"/>Und die, welche Gott fürchtend, richtigen Rechtsspruch ertheilen, die werden von Gott ewigen Endlohn empfahn<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="1" target="#Iudex_17-1.lnote.de.1"/>.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude" ana="#fromGerman">And those who, fearing God, give right judgment will receive from God an eternal final reward.</ab>
        <ab type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#unattributed" corresp="#wit-g-a">And those who (fearing God) judge justly will receive eternal reward from God.</ab>
        <note type="comparison" source="#liebermann" n="476">Isidor, Sent. III 52.3</note>
        <note type="comparisonPrinted" source="#liebermann">ebd. 52, 3</note>
        <note type="editorial">U: translator unrecorded: check; Not in the Quadripartitus. Zupitza suggested ‘edlean’ (reward) for ‘endlean’. Isidore, Sent. III 52.3. In G, Af El follows after half a blank page in the same hand.</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Iudex_17-1.lnote.oe.4" n="4" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">476</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">vgl.</hi> wyrceð <hi rend="italic">III Atr.</hi> 16</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">cf. wyrceð III Atr. 16</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Iudex_17-1.lnote.oe.c" n="c" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">476</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">edlean [<hi rend="italic">Lohn</hi>] <hi rend="italic">schlägt vor ZUPITZA brieflich. Vgl.</hi> praemio <hi rend="italic">Isidor Es folgt nach leerer halber Seite, in ders. Hand</hi> Af. El., <hi rend="italic">oben S.</hi> 26</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">edlean [reward] proposed by ZUPITZA in a letter. Cf. praemio Isidor. There follows, after half a blank page, in the same hand, Af. El., above p. 26</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="erklaerung" xml:id="Iudex_17-1.lnote.de.1" n="1" source="#liebermann-erkl"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">269</biblScope><biblScope unit="column">3</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">Volle Form wäre <hi rend="italic">endelean</hi>; der Ausfall des -<hi rend="italic">e</hi> bei Komposition von <hi rend="italic">ende</hi>- ist sonst erst seit 13. Jh. belegt</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">The full form would be <hi rend="italic">endelean</hi>; the loss of -<hi rend="italic">e</hi> in compounds of <hi rend="italic">ende</hi>- is otherwise attested only from the 13th cent.</seg></note>
      </div>
    </body>
